-- title:
--   Finite chart and base generate the function field
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \geq 1$ (as a natural number with `NeZero N`) and a prime $\ell$, and write $\mathbf{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8), the subring of $\mathbf{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$. Let $S$ be a commutative ring and $\rho \colon \mathbf{Z}_{(\ell)} \to S$ a ring homomorphism, and form the pullback $\mathfrak{X}_S$ of the structure morphism `IgusaScheme.igusaTo N ℓ` from the Igusa scheme (the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the middle chart over the two charts `chartAlgFin N ℓ`, `chartAlgInf N ℓ`, mapped to $\operatorname{Spec} \mathbf{Z}_{(\ell)}$) along $\operatorname{Spec} \rho$. Assume $\mathfrak{X}_S$ is an integral scheme, let $x$ be any point of it, and assume the open subscheme $U \subseteq \mathfrak{X}_S$ obtained as the preimage under the first projection of the image open of the finite chart morphism `IgusaScheme.ιFin N ℓ` is non-empty. Then the function field of $\mathfrak{X}_S$ is generated as a field (its `Subfield.closure` is $\top$) by the union of two sets: the image of `chartAlgFin N ℓ` — the subalgebra of elements of the full modular function field integral over $\mathbf{Z}_{(\ell)}[j]$ — under pulling its global sections back to $U$ and taking germs into the function field, and the image of $S$ under pulling global sections back along the second projection, taking the germ at $x$, and mapping the stalk into the function field.
--
--   This is the statement that the function field of the base change $\mathfrak{X}_S$ of the two-chart Igusa integral model of $X_0(N)$ over $\mathbf{Z}_{(\ell)}$ is generated by the finite ($j$-integral) chart ring together with the constants coming from $S$, the point being that $U$ is a non-empty affine open of an integral scheme with coordinate ring a base change of `chartAlgFin N ℓ`. It is used in the construction of the Deligne–Rapoport-style model package, via [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.phi_algebraMap_stalk_mem_integers_comp_genericPoint`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.phi_algebraMap_stalk_mem_integers_comp_genericPoint), to check that a map defined on generators of the function field lands in the expected ring of integers.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme_subfieldClosure_range_germToFunctionField_union_range_eq_top.lean

